    "Protect native motion duration of mechanisms and numerical examples; do not uniformly compress each scene to voice duration.",
    "Lead time should reveal the object or start its construction; avoid spending it on a blank or barely initialized frame.",
    "Spare time is useful during a multi-step construction and on a settled meaningful result; avoid allocating all of it to a frozen endpoint.",
    "Offsets are proposals and must be clamped or the window enlarged if offset+retainedVoice exceeds planned phase duration; never truncate speech or overlap adjacent voices.",
    "Move every subtitle cue by the same local offset as its associated recorded voice. Do not leave captions before the voice.",
    "When source motion is kept at1x and extra time is needed, prefer a meaningful final plateau after the last event; do not append a frame at a scene boundary that has already faded out.",
